{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo and bulb kit fits my interest in connected home equipment: voice-controlled lighting feels like a useful addition alongside my Fire TV devices.",
    "That kit connects to how I use electronics at home for entertainment and convenience, which makes it a more natural next choice for me."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Ring charging station serves a camera brand I have not bought; my recent Blink camera purchase does not give me Ring batteries to charge.",
    "The internal drives and thermal paste assume a computer upgrade or repair project, while my recent purchases concern streaming, televisions and cameras.",
    "The USB-C cables and wired headphones do not meet an immediate need I have expressed through my purchases.",
    "The mesh WiFi system could support my devices, but owning cameras and streaming equipment does not mean I have a coverage problem that warrants replacing my network."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in electronics seems to have been stretched into an interest in computer parts, even though I am not currently building or upgrading a PC.",
    "Owning connected devices seems to have been treated as a reason to buy accessories or infrastructure without enough attention to compatibility or an actual need."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated Fire TV purchases make additions that fit my home entertainment setup more relevant than unrelated electronics.",
    "The specific equipment I own matters: a camera accessory needs to work with my camera, not simply relate to home security.",
    "I choose moderately and need a concrete use for an item now; a possible future benefit is not enough to make storage, cables or network equipment appealing."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my connected home interests but stretched them into computer projects and accessory needs I do not currently have."
}"}
